hey guys Pete here today I'm gonna do a  general video about the importance of  prophecy and the song and Ice and Fire  novels that the TV show Game of Thrones  is based on I have plans to make videos  that look into individual prophecies in  the coming months while Game of Thrones  is on break so I wanted to make this  first as a primer it will contain  spoilers for everything related to the  Game of Thrones show through season six  and A Song of Ice and Fire books through  Dance with Dragons but that said it's  more food for thought about a way to  think about prophecy then it gives away  big plot points spoiler so prophecy is a  word that by definition means a  statement that something will happen in  the future it can also mean something  specifically tied to a prophet which in  this case would mean something will  happen because it is the will of a  divinity common theme with prophecy is  that it is somewhat vague and open for  interpretation it's a statement that  something will happen in the future but  the exact date time persons involved and  so on aren't exactly known if the  prophecy is related to divine will and  happens to be specific and doesn't come  true there is always wiggle room to say  that the fault lies with the interpreter  or prophet rather than the actual  divinity for a real world example of  this when I was a teenager I used to go  downtown to hang around a record store  in the summertime especially I went  there several times a week it wasn't a  big busy urban place with lots of foot  traffic and at one of the street corners  there was a woman who would show up and  warn everyone that they needed to go  inside their homes for three days my  friends and I called her the three days  lady because that's what she basically  always said three days three days her  prophecy warned that everyone needed to  go home and stay there to repent and get  right with God before the coming  judgement day her prophecy never changed  every day the world was three days away  from ending so to speak she was there  for years and may still do it now for  all that I know but I bring it up to  point out that if you happen to be  someone who encountered her for the  first time three days before an actual  apocalyptic event you might spend the  moment right before your destruction  believing that her prophecy had come  true when I first started reading the  books my thoughts on the prophecy I came  across were that it was just a  distraction and I didn't think any of  the ones we learned would come true this  was backed up by one of the first ones  we hear that Daenerys is unborn son Rago  would turn out to be the stallion that  mounts the world it's a prophecy that is  quickly disproven when Danny  Griese to a blood magic ritual with miry  mazdoor after which Rago dies in the  womb being somewhat cynical by nature  this was all the evidence I needed to  say that prophecy was nothing more than  a sideshow I mean I couldn't dispute  that this world was different than ours  since magic exists not long after the  stallion that mounts the world theory is  discredited Danny walks into her  husband's funeral pyre the one that she  happened to time marry mazdoor - and  where Miriam as Dora is actually burning  alive and where she also placed her  three dragon at the end  Daenerys emerges unburned with three  newly hatched dragons which is a feat  that no one has really been able to do  for like over 150 years she hatched  dragon that's pretty magical and if that  isn't enough think about the shadow baby  Melisandre conjured up this wasn't an  illusion or a trick she literally gave  birth to a shadow that existed in the  world long enough to go over and kill  Renly Baratheon  magic exists in this world and it can't  really be explained away this led to my  point of view being something like okay  this is a world like ours but it also  has magic which is a kind of extra  dimension or force of nature I figured  that all these religions that have  sprung up were similar to the ones in  our world they are there to offer  answers to people who live in a world  where a lot of things happen that just  don't make sense  and this would just then extend to  magical stuff as well  I was happy looking at it this way and  while I still found it interesting to  look at the prophecies I didn't think  any of them were included because they  would eventually be fulfilled over time  I ran into a problem with Melisandre and  I think she is the best example we can  use to understand what the importance of  these prophecies really is Melisandre is  a red priestess who follows the religion  of her lore who is the Lord of Light she  has visions while staring into flames  and she is famous for misinterpreting me  the problem is that pretty much  everything she sees actually comes true  in the stories so she has access to  something and even though she isn't  always spot-on about the details the  visions she has access to are prophetic  hers isn't the only case where this is  true but I use her for the example  because she's a well-known care you  could also look at the ghost of high  heart Maggy the Frog or jochen's green  dreams for similar evidence for a  specific event that we all remember  let's look at Melisandre and Stannis  burning the leeches the details are  slightly different but we see this in  the book and on in the show Melisandre  says she needs King's blood so she gets  some by leaching one of Roberts  faster the leeches are tossed into the  flames with the intent of causing Baylin  greyjoy Joffrey Baratheon and Robb Stark  to all die all of these things come true  which leads Stannis to believe then that  not only can Melisandre see the future  but she can also perform magic that can  lead to him getting things that he wants  to happen what's interesting about this  example is that as readers or viewers we  have much more information than Stannis  does we know that all those events would  have happened anyways and that  Melisandre didn't actually cause them to  happen at all what's more likely is that  the power we know she has being able to  see things that will happen in the  future  led her to already know about these  deaths and that they were going to  happen this put her in a position to  control Stannis by setting up the  burning knowing that his wishes would  come true so this all leads me the two  conclusions related to prophecy in A  Song of Ice and Fire in a game of throne  the first is that more often than not  prophecy is real and while it will  likely be misinterpreted by everyone  involved the underlying events will come  to pass basically it's there for a  reason and it shouldn't be discounted a  quick example of this is Maggy the Frog  telling Cersei her future the things  that she told her have also far come  true and no one else besides her knows  about the prophecy but she has been  letting it guide her decision-making  process all along the second conclusion  is that the real importance of prophecy  in this world is just that well it's  likely to come true without a doubt it  will shape major events and the way  major characters stories develop you  don't have to look further than Robert's  rebellion for evidence of this Rhaegar  Targaryen was obsessed with the prince  that was promised prophecy and it led  him to run off with Lyanna stark this  action led to the realm going to war and  the Targaryen is ultimately losing the  Iron Throne in the end it doesn't matter  if the prophecy is fulfilled what  matters is that Rhaegar believed in it  to the point of making decisions that  change things forever Danice does this  through Melisandre Cersei does this  through the Maggie prophecy and Daenerys  does this in relation to Quaithe and her  house of the undying experience even if  you disagree with my conclusions I think  you'll be able to agree that prophecy is  important and not to mention fun and  interesting to deconstruct I mean people  are always coming up with compelling new  theories based on the open-ended nature  of it all we get to get it wrong just  like the characters and the books get it  wrong and it's just really like a  win-win anyways I hope this gives you  something to think  about and I hope you leave a comment and  let me know what you think do you think  that like say the Izola Ohio Theory's  going to come true or do you think it  doesn't matter because it's really going  to shape the end of the series either  way as mentioned I'll be adding regular  prophecy videos over time so subscribe  to my channel and join the conversation  I also have a giveaway going on for when  I hit 18,000 subscribers I'm giving away  a copy of a night of the Seven Kingdoms  and all you have to do is be a  subscriber and leave a comment in the  video so let me know what your favorite  prophecy is or if you think prophecies  all bull or who do you think is over hi  is whatever just leave a comment and  you'll have a chance to win so thanks  for watching I'll talk to you soon
 

